        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Fukusa (gift cover) of tapestry-weave silk velvet (tsuzure birôdo), a complex and time-consuming technique in which extra, different coloured, pile warps create the pattern. The design is of a cockerel, hen and chicks in muted tones of black, brown, blue and white. There are seals woven into the cover on the left, and the border contains paulownia motifs."@en ;
